# Call-site ledger of tinytag at c123836e950a897bd4bbee04d3700bec8762ca27.
#
# The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in macro-benchmark/README.md;
# tinytag.md shows how this ledger applies them. The package is one module
# (tinytag/tinytag.py) and the command line (tinytag/__main__.py). The parser
# classes _ID3, _MPEG, _Ogg, _Wave, _Flac, _ASF, _MP4 and _Aiff are private
# (C); a client reaches them only through TinyTag.get. File objects: the
# client's file_obj is opaque (annotated BinaryIO, an abstract type; B4, B5);
# the package's own files are the io.BufferedReader that get opens and the
# io.BytesIO objects that the parsers make (tinytag.md, "File objects").
# OtherFields and OtherImages subclass dict at run time (line 56).
default reject tinytag.tinytag.Image.__repr__: no package code formats, prints or converts an Image; the formatted and printed values are strs, bytes, ints, floats, bools, lists of str, exceptions (OSError, TinyTagException and its subclasses, which define no __str__ or __repr__) and dicts of those

